      "body": "Resolves #41230.\n\n## Summary\nDocument the metrics aggregation semantics of the NIXL KV connector, which were previously undocumented and caused user confusion in multi-rank (TP > 1) deployments.\n\n## Changes\n- `vllm/distributed/kv_transfer/kv_connector/v1/nixl/stats.py`: expanded `NixlKVConnectorStats` docstring explaining that stats are aggregated across all TP ranks before `reduce()` computes summary stats, with per-metric semantics (Num successful transfers / Avg MB per transfer / Throughput / P90); clarifying comments in `aggregate()` and `reduce()`.\n- `vllm/distributed/kv_transfer/kv_connector/v1/metrics.py`: documented the `observe()` -> `aggregate()` -> `reduce()` -> `log()` pipeline on `KVConnectorLogging`, noting stats arrive pre-aggregated across workers.\n\n## Test plan\nDocs-only change (docstrings/comments); no functional code touched.\n\nAI assistance disclosure: this documentation patch was drafted with AI assistance and reviewed by the contributor.",
